# tools/l/lasso_select_witness.rish -- given a query POLYGON (a free-form LASSO), name every OBJECT it covers, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/hit_test.rye names the ONE object under a POINT, image/region_select.rye names EVERY
# object a RECTANGLE covers; this rung names EVERY object an ARBITRARY POLYGON covers -- the lasso / free-select primitive a surface
# runs when a keeper draws a loop. Exact integers, NO float, NO tolerance -- a pixel is covered when it is foreground AND inside the
# polygon, decided by an even-odd ray cast in DOUBLED coordinates; the label map is the arbiter, each object's bounding box only a
# prefilter.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal, the rectangle crux one shape freer: a bounding box that OVERLAPS is necessary but not
# sufficient, AND a CONCAVE lasso can EXCLUDE an object that any convex query would include. A right-pointing concave chevron whose
# tip covers one object and whose notch opens around another selects exactly the tip object, though the chevron's box overlaps BOTH
# (poly_bbox_overlap_count 2) and its convex hull holds the notch object too -- every pixel of that object falls in the concavity,
# outside the loop; a small quad drawn around the notch object selects it exactly (completeness); a whole-scene lasso selects every
# object ascending; a lasso off the map is a valid empty selection; a degenerate polygon refuses DegeneratePoly; determinism. No
# network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/lasso_select_witness.rish

say "lasso_select: Language EN -- Season G polygon-to-object-set select; a pixel is covered when foreground AND inside the polygon by an even-odd ray cast in DOUBLED coordinates; the label map is the arbiter, each object's bounding box only a prefilter; NO float, NO tolerance."
say "lasso_select: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns the point-in-polygon arbiter and the box-overlap prefilter reads; label owns the at arbiter, scene_manifest owns the per-object rows, regions owns the bounding box, contour owns the Point vertex. No plane of its own, no pixel written -- a reading, not a render."
say "lasso_select: Lens TAME -- a lasso carries three to max_poly_vertices vertices; the candidate scan runs components times under label_max_pixels; the arbiter scan reads the polygon's box clamped to the map under qoi's pixel ceiling, each pixel testing at most max_poly_vertices edges; a degenerate polygon refuses DegeneratePoly, an off-map lasso selects empty; all-or-nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/lasso_select"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/lasso_select.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "lasso_select: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "lasso_select: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "lasso_select: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-lasso-select" else "lasso_select: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "a pixel is covered exactly when it is foreground AND inside the polygon" else "lasso_select: the foreground-and-inside rule did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "an EVEN-ODD ray cast in DOUBLED coordinates" else "lasso_select: the even-odd doubled-coordinate device did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "i128 CROSS-MULTIPLICATION, exact integers, NO float and NO tolerance" else "lasso_select: the exact-arithmetic claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the DECISIVE concavity crux, strictly sharper than the rectangle marquee" else "lasso_select: the decisive concavity crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "selects EXACTLY the tip object" else "lasso_select: the tip-only selection did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the chevron's bounding box overlaps BOTH objects (poly_bbox_overlap_count reads 2)" else "lasso_select: the box-overlaps-both prefilter did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "its convex hull holds the notch object too" else "lasso_select: the convex-hull-holds-it claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the capability a marquee or any convex query could never carve" else "lasso_select: the marquee-cannot-carve claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "completeness proves the exclusion is geometry not a blind spot" else "lasso_select: the completeness case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a whole-scene lasso selects every object ascending, label 1 then label 2" else "lasso_select: the whole-scene case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a lasso off the map is a valid empty selection" else "lasso_select: the off-map case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a two-vertex degenerate polygon refuses DegeneratePoly having read nothing" else "lasso_select: the DegeneratePoly refusal did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the same lasso reads the same selection twice" else "lasso_select: determinism did not print"

say "lasso_select: GREEN on metal -- given a polygon, the lasso select names every object it truly covers, carving out an object a concave loop excludes though its box and convex hull hold it, and grabbing it exactly when the loop is drawn around it; refusals by name, determinism. Season G open-media."
